**\n- Uses `asyncio.Semaphore` to limit concurrent execution to `max_concurrent`\n- When Ctrl+C (KeyboardInterrupt) is pressed, running tasks continue and their cleanup code (try/finally blocks) still executes\n- Wraps each task with semaphore acquisition so they respect the concurrency limit\n\n**How cleanup works:**\nWhen a KeyboardInterrupt occurs, asyncio will cancel pending tasks. Tasks that are already running will receive a `CancelledError`, but their `finally` blocks will still execute, allowing cleanup code to run properly.\n\nThe function can be imported as:\n```python\nfrom run import run_tasks\n```\n\nExample usage:\n```python\nimport asyncio\nfrom run import run_tasks\n\nasync def my_task():\n    try:\n        # do work\n        await asyncio.sleep(5)\n    finally:\n        # cleanup code runs even on interrupt\n        print(\"Cleaning up!\")\n\nasyncio.run(run_tasks([my_task, my_task], max_concurrent=2))\n```","ttft_ms":35037,"type":"result","duration_ms":40112,"uuid":"1ca86abb-eb28-4a17-964a-6f66fab02b90","ttft_stream_ms":704,"time_to_request_ms":82,"queued_turn_count":0}
